atlas identity

architecture actor-graph
  canonical_name ActorGraph
  family identity
  domain Identity / Institutional Capacity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Who is this real-world actor, and for which profile is that identity verified?
  purpose Real actors with identifier assertions, observations, corroboration, and per-profile verification. The verified-for law is the point.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Actor
  node_types IdentifierAssertion
  node_types Corroboration
  node_types VerificationProfile
  edge_types asserts
  edge_types corroborates
  edge_types affiliated_with
  state_types asserted
  state_types observed
  state_types corroborated
  state_types verified_for
  state_types contradicted
  invariant asserted_via_email is not verified_for(ACM.editor)
  forbidden_inference email sender -> verified institutional role
  forbidden_inference affiliation -> authority
  forbidden_inference identity similarity -> same actor
  native_format graf
  command BonfyreEntity
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/actors.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/pack_loader.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_actors.py
  source_lineage capitalgym crm relationships

architecture hash-identity
  canonical_name HashIdentityGraph
  family identity
  domain Identity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Are these byte/content objects identical?
  purpose Content-addressed identity: bytes -> digest -> Merkle membership. Used by artifacts, packs, model weights, receipts.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ContentObject
  edge_types hashes_to
  edge_types merkle_member_of
  forbidden_inference same bytes -> same derivational meaning
  native_format graf
  command BonfyreHash
  source_path cmd/BonfyreHash
  source_lineage identity federation seed
